course: dictionary
lesson: 2717
title: Dimmer: less bright
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dimmer is the comparison form of dim. When two lights are compared, the one that gives out less light is the dimmer one. «The light grew dimmer as the batteries ran down.» Here dimmer means the light gave out less light than before.
explain: Dimmer can also be a noun, meaning a dimmer switch. This switch lets you make a light brighter or less bright, so a room can be bright for reading or soft for a film. Look for the words around dimmer to tell which meaning is in use: a light that is growing dimmer, or a switch you turn.
explain: Dimmer has a second, informal meaning: less clever. It is an unkind word for a person, so do not use it to call someone names. In this lesson, focus on the meaning about light.
fact: Dimmer means less bright.
fact: A dimmer switch lets you make a light brighter or less bright.
fact: Dimmer is the comparison form of dim, so use it to compare two things: one patch of light can be dimmer than another.
fact: «Tilt the torch and the spot spreads out bigger and dimmer.» A torch held at a slant makes a bigger, dimmer patch.
fact: Informally, dimmer can mean less clever, and it is unkind when used that way.
exercise: «The light grew dimmer as night fell.» What does dimmer mean here? | Closer to the ground | Brighter and warmer | Louder | *Less bright
exercise: «A dimmer switch lets you make a room cosy for a film.» What is a dimmer switch? | A switch that turns the water on | A switch that makes a loud noise | A switch that only works on the television | *A switch that changes how bright a light is
exercise: «Saturn's rings shine brightly, and dark rock would look much dimmer.» Which would look less bright than the ice? | Ice grains | Water ice | *Dark rock | Fresh snow
test: A torch pointed straight down makes a small, bright spot, and a torch held at a slant makes a bigger patch. Which patch is dimmer? | The small spot | Both are equally bright | *The bigger patch | Neither patch has any light
test: «If a Cepheid looks dimmer than its pulse says it really is, it must be farther away.» If a star looks dimmer than it really is, where is it? | Pulsing faster | Brighter than before | Closer to Earth | *Farther away
exam: The lamp grew ___ as the battery ran low. Choose the correct word. | *Dimmer | Warmer | Louder | Brighter
